WEBVTT

00:00:00.724 --> 00:00:01.397
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:01.704 --> 00:00:03.191
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> A wind-up torch.

00:00:03.644 --> 00:00:09.452
This torch works using a dynamo. The battery is recharged by winding the handle.

00:00:09.739 --> 00:00:14.387
It’s perfect for emergencies, or in places where there is no electricity.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.229
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:18.318
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> A shoe that grows.

00:00:18.978 --> 00:00:24.841
In many places, parents can’t afford to buy new shoes when their children’s feet grow.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:32.298
This comfortable, long-lasting shoe is completely adjustable, and can expand up to five sizes.

00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:33.880
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:39.972
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> A solar hearing aid. Over 600 million people need hearing aids,

00:00:40.237 --> 00:00:44.640
but at least half can’t afford to buy them, or to replace the batteries.

00:00:45.135 --> 00:00:46.452
This cost-effective,

00:00:46.497 --> 00:00:51.987
eco-friendly device has a rechargeable battery which lasts for two to three years.